# Dated snapshot copies of the installer. Git's own history replaces the
# manual dated-snapshot ritual, so these pre-git artifacts are not tracked.
# The live working file Void_Linux_Installer.sh (no version segment) is NOT
# ignored and is the tracked source of truth.
snapshots/

# Generated from INSTALL_PROMPTS.md the same way the installer prompts would;
# regenerable via chromium's headless print-to-pdf. Keep only the .md source.
INSTALL_PROMPTS.pdf

# Editor / OS noise
*.swp
*~
.DS_Store

# Debug artifacts from real-hardware installs / LightDM greeter & snapper
# probes. Investigative scratch, not part of the shipped tool. Kept on disk,
# excluded from git. Debug/* (not Debug/) lets git descend and re-include the
# committed exceptions below.
Debug/*
# ...but Debug/check-heredocs.sh IS committed — it is the reproducible
# heredoc-lint gate (bash -n + shellcheck over every extracted generated body)
# that AGENTS.md's Validation section mandates. Re-unignore exactly this file.
!Debug/check-heredocs.sh
# ...and Debug/check-defaults.sh IS committed — the reproducible check that
# the [PROMPT-DEFAULTS] block stays consistent (every DEFAULT_* declared AND
# wired, no stray references), per AGENTS.md's Validation section. Re-unignore.
!Debug/check-defaults.sh
# ...and Debug/check-pkg-preflight.sh IS committed — the reproducible
# [PKG-PREFLIGHT] (Beta-v2.9.40) drift-guard that fails when a chroot
# package name is added to the installer without also being added to the
# PKG_PREFLIGHT candidate list (crash #005 regression guard). Re-unignore.
!Debug/check-pkg-preflight.sh
# ...and Debug/check-nvram-prompt.sh IS committed — the Version-3.0.01
# [LIMINE-NVRAM-LABEL]/[LIMINE-NVRAM-PROMPT-MOVE] prompt suite: 23 cases over
# the prompt block it extracts VERBATIM from the installer (marker-based line
# resolution, so it cannot drift when line numbers move). Re-unignore.
!Debug/check-nvram-prompt.sh
# ...and Debug/check-bios-boot.sh IS committed — the Version-3.1.00
# [BIOS-BOOT] gate: 42 static checks that every firmware-dependent construct
# sits behind an explicit $BOOT_MODE gate and that the BIOS wiring
# (detection -> geometry -> budget -> chroot_env -> carve -> Stage 2 ->
# generator -> records) is complete. Re-unignore.
!Debug/check-bios-boot.sh
# ...and Debug/qemu-matrix/ IS committed — the QEMU/SeaBIOS+OVMF validation
# harness behind the Version-3.1.00 runtime claims (scripts + a README only:
# the ISO, extracted kernel/initrd and per-case images/logs stay out of git).
# Debug/* matches direct children, so unignoring the directory is enough.
!Debug/qemu-matrix/
# ...but keep byte-compiled droppings out of the harness directory.
Debug/qemu-matrix/__pycache__/
# ...and the live kernel/initrd the harness boots (~260 MB, extracted from the
# ISO once — see Debug/qemu-matrix/README.md for the one-line recipe).
Debug/qemu-matrix/live-extract/
# ...plus the medium it boots and the per-case output (qcow2, logs, PNGs):
# both default INSIDE the harness dir, and the ISO symlink's TARGET is a local
# path the deny-list would block, so neither may ever reach an index.
Debug/qemu-matrix/void-live.iso
Debug/qemu-matrix/artifacts/
# ...and the YubiKey possession-only validation kit (probe + protocol) is
# committed so it survives until the real-hardware run happens.
!Debug/yk_validation/
# ...and the boot/validation review list is committed the same way — it is
# the tracker for real-hardware findings that need a root-cause (Entry #1:
# ENCRYPT boot-unlock passphrase rejection).
!Debug/REVIEW.md
# ...and the one-page live-validation runbook (Beta-v2.9.38 MULTI-FS scenarios
# A-E + batched pending items) is committed — it is the target-medium proof
# checklist for the multi-filesystem data regions era.
!Debug/LIVE-VALIDATION-RUNBOOK.md
# ...and the COSMIC grey-screen validation kit (on-box repro/repair script,
# diagnose bundle, triage + session-log snapshots) is committed so the
# hardware-validated Beta-v2.9.10/11 cookbook survives the box reboots.
!Debug/Cosmic-Greeter/
